== Sauce ==

In a #small bowl{}, combine @pumpkin puree{15%oz}(1 can; or 12 oz thawed frozen winter squash puree), @Parmesan cheese{1/2%cup}(grated; pecorino also works), @garlic{2%cloves}(minced), @smoked paprika{3/4%tsp}(or regular paprika), @ground cumin{1/2%tsp}, @ground nutmeg{1/4%tsp}, @salt{1/4%tsp}, and @black pepper{1/4%tsp}. Stir until well combined. Set aside.

== Toppings ==

Trim stems from @Brussels sprouts{3/4%lb}. Shred in a #food processor{} with the shredding disk, or halve and thinly slice with a #knife{}. Toss with @extra-virgin olive oil{1%tbsp}.

== Glaze ==

In a #small saucepan{}, combine @balsamic vinegar{1/2%cup} and @light brown sugar{2%tsp}(firmly packed). Simmer over medium heat until syrupy and reduced to about 2 tablespoons, about ~{6%minutes}. Set aside.

== Assemble & bake ==

Preheat the #oven{} to 400°F. Line two #baking sheets{} with parchment or foil.

Spread the squash/pumpkin sauce over each @naan{4}(Trader Joe's works well; garlic naan is fine), leaving about a 1/2-inch border. Top with the shredded Brussels sprouts, @goat cheese{1/4%cup}(crumbled, ~1 oz), and @hazelnuts{1/4%cup}(chopped, ~1 oz). Arrange the flatbreads on the sheets.

Bake until the crust is golden and the cheese begins to melt, about ~{10%minutes}. Drizzle with the balsamic glaze to serve.

> Annotated from *The Runner's World Vegetarian Cookbook*. See [transcription review #12](https://github.com/Levison/cookbook/issues/12).
